      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1762948133469,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Each user has a profile page. Some of it is automatically populated based on the login mechanism. The rest of the fields will have to be\nmanually added. \n*username and password are relevant only if you create your own account but not when you authenticate with CLARIAH or ORCID (is it\ntrue?).",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "xKZ-mkE9LjI-f7mxgB1hm",
      "originalText": "Each user has a profile page. Some of it is automatically populated based on the login mechanism. The rest of the fields will have to be manually added. \n*username and password are relevant only if you create your own account but not when you authenticate with CLARIAH or ORCID (is it true?).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "R23YM53M-OBFG2ApUdm2r",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6489.4704068025585,
      "y": 3782.303378614117,
      "width": 921.29052734375,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b88",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1806889273,
      "version": 437,
      "versionNonce": 547313241,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1762949173784,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Toys, as cultural artefacts, offer a unique lens through which we can critically examine\nsocietal norms, challenge stereotypes, explore notions of gender and social behaviour,\nscrutinise body image, consider aspects of race, ethnicity, and engage with the impacts of\ntechnological innovation and geographical contexts on play. This project delves into the\nbroader social, cultural, and historical contexts that shape and are shaped by the act of\nplaying, and becomes a repository of narratives, utilising toys as symbolic surrogates to\narticulate interconnected and non-linear stories.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Toys, as cultural artefacts, offer a unique lens through which we can critically examine societal norms, challenge stereotypes, explore notions of gender and social behaviour, scrutinise body image, consider aspects of race, ethnicity, and engage with the impacts of technological innovation and geographical contexts on play. This project delves into the broader social, cultural, and historical contexts that shape and are shaped by the act of playing, and becomes a repository of narratives, utilising toys as symbolic surrogates to articulate interconnected and non-linear stories.\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
